course: dictionary
lesson: 15936
title: Unrestricted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unrestricted means without limits, rules or controls. It means you are free to do, have or use as much as you want. Think of it as the opposite of blocked or limited.
explain: «The museum has an unrestricted view of the sea from its roof.» Nothing gets in the way, so you can see the whole sea. The word tells you that nothing blocks the view.
explain: «Our school ticket is unrestricted, so we can use it on any day.» The ticket has no limits on the days you can use it. Read the words around unrestricted to check: are there any limits in the sentence? If there are none, the word means no limits.
fact: Unrestricted means without limits, rules or controls.
fact: «Unrestricted access» means you can go in or use something with no limits.
fact: «Unrestricted view» means nothing blocks what you can see.
fact: «The school blocks some websites, so its internet is not unrestricted.» Schools use filters to keep children safe online.
fact: A quick check is to swap in the word «free»: if the sentence still makes sense, unrestricted probably means free from limits.
exercise: «The museum has an unrestricted view of the sea from its roof.» What does unrestricted mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Only open on Sundays | *Nothing blocks the view | Very small
exercise: «Our school ticket is unrestricted, so we can use it on any day.» What does the ticket allow? | It costs nothing at all | *It can be used at any time | It is only for grown-ups | It must be printed in red
exercise: «The school blocks some websites, so its internet is not unrestricted.» What does this sentence tell you? | The internet is very fast | *Some websites are blocked, so there are limits | Everyone must pay for the internet
test: Which phrase means that nothing blocks what you can see? | Restricted ticket | Unrestricted rules | *Unrestricted view
test: Is unrestricted another word for small? | *No, it means without limits, rules or controls | Yes, it means tiny | Yes, it means very quiet
exam: Which sentence uses unrestricted correctly? | My shoes are unrestricted because they are too small | *The park gives unrestricted access to the lake, so anyone can go there | Unrestricted is a colour of paint that dries fast | The cat was unrestricted, so it had to sit in its basket
